## About this document

The SBO License is a copyleft license written for Stellar Blade Online (SBO),
a mod for the game Stellar Blade. Sections 0 to 12 and 14 to 17 reuse, with
changes, the wording of version 3 of the GNU General Public License,
copyright (C) 2007 Free Software Foundation, Inc. The SBO License is a
different license. It is not the GNU General Public License, the Free
Software Foundation has neither written nor endorsed it, and no version of it
lets anyone convey a covered work under a GNU license.

## Purpose

This License lets everyone except the Excluded Parties run, study, change and
share the Program free of charge. Anyone who conveys the Program, changed or
not, must pass on the same rights, the source code and these terms. The
License differs from the license it is based on in these places. It gives no
rights to Excluded Parties as section 0 defines them: the parties listed in
Appendix A, the people and organizations linked to them, and the services and
programs they run (section 13). It grants no right to the project's names and
logo for modified versions that are released (section 18). No one but the
Licensor may sell a covered work or charge for it (section 20). No one may
run a covered work as a server for other people without the Licensor's
written permission, though hosting or joining a game while you play stays
free, and anyone who modifies a covered work and lets other people use the
modified version over a network must offer them its source code (section
21). Only the Licensor publishes new versions of it (section 14). As an
agreement, it is governed by Belgian law (section 19). Sections 0, 2, 4, 6,
7, 9, 10 and 11 carry the changes that follow from these.

