  4) that Appendix A names or describes as part of an entry; or

  5) that a person or organization under item (b), including staff, runs,
  or ran when it was set up, and that a party listed under (a) or (e) links
  to, promotes or presents to its users as a place to get, install or update
  mods.

This includes software that runs on a user's own computer, such as a
launcher or mod manager, together with the catalog, servers and update
channels that feed it. A general-purpose service that an affiliate of such a
party runs, such as code hosting, file storage, video hosting, search or a
social network, is an Excluded Service only to the extent that the party or
the affiliate uses it to offer, list, host, download, install or update
mods.

A person who uses an Excluded Service only for their own purposes, for
example to install mods on their own computer, does not act for it. A person
or organization is not an Excluded Party only because it has an account on
an Excluded Service, publishes there its own works that are not covered
works, or uses an Excluded Service for anything other than a covered work.
Section 13 states what happens to a copy of a covered work that an Excluded
Service makes or handles.

"Project Names" has the meaning given in section 18. To "charge" has the
meaning given in section 20, and to run a covered work "as a server" has the
meaning given in section 21.

An interactive user interface displays "Appropriate Legal Notices" to the
extent that it includes a convenient and prominently visible feature that
