   covered only for the copies and builds of it that such a person or
   organization makes, changes, configures or bundles; for the extensions,
   plug-ins, modules and settings for it that are made to work with the
   platform, catalog or accounts that this entry covers, whoever made them,
   or that such a person or organization supplies; and to the extent that it
   gets mods from, or sends mods to, that platform, catalog or accounts, as
   item 3 of the definition of "Excluded Service" states. A program is made
   for AyakaMods when it is made at the request of, or under an agreement
   with, a person or organization under items (a) to (e) of that definition,
   or is made to work only or mainly with the platform, catalog or accounts
   that this entry covers, whoever made it.

The Licensor may publish, at the publication address named in section 0,
notices that name further domains, accounts, programs, companies or
successors that it considers covered by an entry above. Such a notice adds
no party. Whether an entry covers a person, organization, service or
program is decided under section 0 and this appendix.

## How to apply this License to your work

To license a work you wrote under this License, put a notice at the start of
each source file. The notice gives the copyright, says that the work comes
with no warranty, and says where the full License is. Each file needs at
least the copyright line and a pointer to the License.

    <name of the work and one line on what it does>
    Copyright (C) <year> <name of the copyright holder>
    SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-SBO-1.0-or-later

    You may use, study, change and share this work under the SBO License,
    version 1.0 or, at your option, any later version that the Licensor
    publishes. The License gives no rights to the Excluded Parties it
    defines, including the parties listed in its Appendix A. It does not
    let anyone sell the work or charge for it, or run it as a server for
    other people without the Licensor's written permission. Hosting or
    joining a game session while you play is not running a server.

    This work comes with NO WARRANTY, to the extent the law allows.
    Sections 15 to 17 of the License give the details.

    The License, with its Appendix A, comes with this work in the file
    LICENSE. It is also published at
    https://github.com/MotherSphere/stellar-blade-coop.

To license a work under version 1.0 only, write "version 1.0" in place of
"version 1.0 or, at your option, any later version that the Licensor
publishes", and use the identifier `LicenseRef-SBO-1.0`.

Put the full text of this License, with Appendix A, in a file named LICENSE
at the top of the work. Add a way to contact you.

If the work shows a notice when it starts, or has an about or credits
screen, show there the work's name, the copyright line, that it comes with
no warranty, that it is licensed under the SBO License, and how to read the
License.

`LicenseRef-SBO-1.0` and `LicenseRef-SBO-1.0-or-later` are identifiers of the
form that SPDX uses for licenses outside its license list. They are not
registered anywhere.

If you write code for an employer or a school, check that you hold the
copyright in it, or get a written waiver from them, before you license it.
